  "body": "It's annoying to deal with `window.onload`, since your async code might not know whether it's run before or after the load event has fired.  jQuery makes this easy with its `$.ready()` function, which functions in a promise-like manner.\n\nSo anyway, let's add a `.ready` promise to `Document`.\n",
